   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law and the state finance law, in relation to providing for taxpayer gifts for heart disease prevention and education and establishing the heart disease prevention and education fund",
    "basePrintNo": "A3577",
    "basePrintNoStr": "A3577-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A3577A\n\nTITLE  OF BILL:   An act to amend the tax law and the state finance law,\nin relation to providing for taxpayer gifts for heart disease prevention\nand education and establishing the heart disease prevention  and  educa-\ntion fund\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo  provide  that  taxpayers may donate for the benefit of heart disease\nprevention and education from their income tax return. Also  establishes\nthe heart disease prevention and education fund.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nA new section, 209-e, is added to the Tax Law.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThe  Tax  Law is amended by adding a new section, 209-e, which defines a\ntaxpayer's choice of contributing to the support of  the  heart  disease\neducation and prevention fund from their income tax return.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn  joint  custody  of  the commissioner of taxation and finance and the\ncomptroller, a fund for heart disease prevention and education shall  be\nestablished.  These  funds  will consist of all revenues received by the\ndepartment of taxation and finance. Nothing  contained  in  these  funds\nshall prevent the state from receiving grants, gifts or bequests for the\npurpose  of  supporting  the  funds.  Donations  for  the funds shall be\nexpended only for the purpose of supporting heart disease prevention and\neducation program administration and implementation. It shall be  admin-\nistered by the Mary Lasker Heart and Hypertension Institute. The commis-\nsioner  of  health  shall  ensure  that  all donations received during a\nfiscal year are expended prior to the end of the fiscal year.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: A6896-A committed to  rules  in  2004.  A6797\npassed  assembly, delivered to senate and referred to investigations and\ngovernment operations on 05/24/06.  A4415 passed assembly, delivered  to\nsenate  and  referred  to  investigations  and  government operations on\n3/3/08.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:  None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
