    "lawCode": "Add §§209-H & 630-c, Tax L; add §89-h, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A3577B\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law and the state finance law,\nin relation to providing for taxpayer gifts for heart disease\nprevention and education and establishing the heart disease prevention\nand education fund\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:  To provide that taxpayers may donate\nfor the benefit of heart disease prevention and education from their\nincome tax return. Also establishes the heart disease prevention and\neducation fund.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:  A new section, 209-e, is added to the\nTax Law.\n\nEXISTING LAW:  The Tax Law is amended by adding a new section, 209-e,\nwhich defines a taxpayer's choice of contributing to the support of\nthe heart disease education and prevention fund from their income tax\nreturn.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  In joint custody of the commissioner of taxation and\nfinance and the comptroller, a fund for heart disease prevention and\neducation shall be established. These funds will consist of all\nrevenues received by the department of taxation and finance. Nothing\ncontained in these funds shall prevent the state from receiving\ngrants, gifts or bequests for the purpose of supporting the funds.\nDonations for the funds shall be expended only for the purpose of\nsupporting heart disease prevention and education program\nadministration and implementation. It shall be administered by the\ndepartment of health through the Mary Lasker Heart and Hypertension\nInstitute.\n\nThe commissioner of health shall ensure that all donations received\nduring a fiscal year are expended prior to the end of the fiscal year.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: A6896-A committed to rules in 2004. A6797\npassed assembly, delivered to senate and referred to investigations\nand government operations on 05/24/06. A4415 passed assembly,\ndelivered to senate and referred to investigations and government\noperations on 3/3/08. A3577-A passed assembly, delivered to senate and\nreferred to investigations and government operations on 03/18/10.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:  None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
